 ## Background
-The Tabulated BSSRDF method is described in the context of physically based rendering for volume scattering [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the dimensionality problem of the BSSRDF by leveraging the fact that $\sigma_t$ and $r$ can be combined into a single dimensionless parameter $r_{optical}$, and that $\eta$ and $g$ can be fixed for a given material [S1, unofficial]. This approach is part of the broader effort to efficiently simulate subsurface scattering in computer graphics.
